ifts in snatch and clean &amp; jerk determined placement.  Ties broken by lightest bodyweight."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "China’s Wang Mingjuan was the 2002-03 World Champion and the world record holder but she was bypassed for the 2004 team by " [:a {:href ""} "Li Zhao"] ", who immediately became the favorite. However, the lead after the snatch was taken by Turkey’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/103516"} "Nurcan Taylan"] ", the 2004 European Champion, who broke the world record with a lift of 95.0 kg, followed by another world record of 97.5 kg. When Taylan cleaned &amp; jerked 112.5 kg, Li was forced to try 120.0 kg in the clean &amp; jerk but missed badly on two attempts, giving the gold medal to Taylan. Taylan became the first Turkish woman to win a gold medal, which brought her a $273,000 reward from the state and a phone call from the Turkish President. Fourth-place was initially given to Myanmar’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/103519"} "Nan Aye Khine"] " but she ran afoul of the doping tests."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103516"} "Nurcan Taylan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUR.png"}] "TUR"]] [:td {} "210.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103517"} "Li Zhuo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "205.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""}